## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design per-tenant budgets, dynamic throttling, and robust rollback strategies in a multi-tenant, latency-sensitive service.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant SLOs and budgets
- Burn rate calculation and budget ledger
- Edge throttling (token bucket) and graceful degradation
- Canary rollouts and automated rollback
- Observability with per-tenant metrics and PromQL

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: update per-tenant budget on each request
function onRequest(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['tenant-id'];
  const now = Date.now();
  const budget = ledger.getBudget(tenant);
  if (budget.remaining <= 0) throttle(req, tenant);
  else { forward(req); ledger.consume(tenant, estimateCost(req)); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this system under simulated traffic bursts?
- What thresholds would you choose for alerting and auto-rollback cadence?

## Why This Is Asked

Telemetry quality is critical for root cause analysis and cross-service tracing; this checks practical skills for CI, instrumentation, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry integrity, trace propagation, OpenTelemetry, CI gates, canary deployments
- Error budgets and dashboards alignment
- Synthetic validation and fallback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry middleware for trace propagation
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

function ensureTraceId(req, res, next) {
  const carrier = propagation.createExtractHeadersCarrier(req.headers);
  const ctx = propagation.extract(context.active(), carrier);

  if (!trace.getSpan(ctx).spanContext().traceId) {
    const tracer = trace.getTracer('default');
    const span = tracer.startSpan('fallback-trace');
    propagation.inject(context.active(), carrier);
  }
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure telemetry coverage and what would trigger a rollback?
- What trade-offs exist when dropping events missing trace_id?

## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates a candidate's ability to design resilient, multi-region metrics pipelines that can withstand regional failures while maintaining data integrity and SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-region ingestion architecture with blast radius containment
- Per-tenant quotas, token-bucket throttling, and bounded local buffering
- Idempotent writes with deterministic IDs and backpressure signaling
- Circuit breakers and automated regional failover mechanisms
- Observability metrics: ingress latency, drop rate, max replay delay
- Adaptive sampling for surge handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// pseudo-code for idempotent write with backpressure
function writeWithBackpressure(metric) {
  const id = generateDeterministicId(metric);
  if (isBackpressureActive()) {
    bufferLocally(metric);
    return;
  }
  return idempotentWrite(id, metric);
}
```
